Day 72 and 73 /100 of hashtag#DrGViswanathanChallenge
Solved LeetCode 653 – Two Sum IV today!

- Approach:
I used a HashSet to keep track of values already visited.
For every node:
 Check whether k - node.val already exists in the set. 
 If yes → a valid pair exists. 
 Otherwise, add the current value and continue through the tree. 

Time: O(n) 
Space: O(n) 
 -Takeaways:
 HashSet makes pair-sum checking efficient. 
 BST properties aren't always necessary when a simple traversal + HashSet gives an optimal solution. 
